{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection","lean:module:QOU.Mass.PsdDetOneTrace","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor_zero","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L178-L185","doc":"**The floor at `n = 0` is `1`**, so the strict step above cannot start\nthere — recorded so the `n ≠ 0` hypothesis is checkable rather than trusted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor_strictAnti_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor_strictAnti_step","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L151-L176","doc":"**The floor is strictly decreasing for `n ≥ 1`.**\n\nBy the recurrence, `traceFloor q (n+1) < traceFloor q n` reduces to\n`[n+2]_q < [2]_q [n+1]_q = [n+2]_q + [n]_q`, i.e. to `0 < [n]_q`.\n\nThe hypothesis `n ≠ 0` is load-bearing, not defensive: at `n = 0` both sides\nare `1` and the strict inequality is false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.qb_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.qb_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L139-L149","doc":"**The three-term recurrence** `[2]_q · [m+1]_q = [m+2]_q + [m]_q`.\n\nThis is what makes the decay below exactly the statement `[n]_q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.traceFloor","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The floor `[n+1]_q / [2]_q^n` — the convention-D weight of the trivial\nblock at `n` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.pairing_ge_one_of_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.pairing_ge_one_of_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L98-L125","doc":"**The bound that supersedes the floor below: the pairing is at least `1`.**\n\n`pairing_ge_weight_of_psdFeasible` keeps one term of the pairing and discards\nthe rest as merely non-negative. They are not merely non-negative: on a\ndeterminant-one block a PSD matrix has trace at least its dimension\n(`PsdDetOneTrace.card_le_trace_of_det_one`), so each term is at least\n`y l * d l` — and those sum to `1`, because that sum IS the Markov\nnormalisation `tr_M(1) = 1`.\n\nThe determinant hypothesis is not an assumption about the candidate but a\nproperty of the γγ construction: `σᵢ` and `σᵢ₊₁` are conjugate in the braid\ngroup, so their block images share a determinant and every vertex — hence\nevery word — has determinant `1` in every block. Measured to `1e-39` in the\ncompanion probe; it enters here as a hypothesis per §3b.\n\nThe bound is **tight**: the empty word is the identity in every block, so\nevery trace equals its dimension and the sum is exactly `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.pairing_ge_weight_of_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GammaGammaTraceFloor.pairing_ge_weight_of_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GammaGammaTraceFloor.lean#L76-L96","doc":"**A PSD-feasible candidate's Frobenius pairing is bounded below by the\nweight of any block whose character it pins at `1`.**\n\nThis is the SDP half of the ruling doing work: `PSDFeasible` forces every\n`(B.proj w l).trace` to be non-negative, so with non-negative weights every\nterm of `Σ_l y l * χ_l(w)` is non-negative and the sum dominates the `l₀`\nterm, which is `y l₀ * 1`.\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly the three ingredients and no more: weight\nnon-negativity, PSD feasibility, and the distinguished character value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}